# Two constants hold descriptors of the same names, which are one layout: what that layout is seen to hold under `value` is what either lays. What each lays is what the body that defines stores THROUGH THAT CONSTANT:
# `_z` is expected to hold an Inner and `_w` an Other, and the reads behind them are tested for that. Both have the name `n`, so the name alone says nothing. f6 = run
# RUN: link fields mechanisms=all
# CHECK-NOT: "_z" proven
# RUN(HELD): link held fields mechanisms=all
# HELD: "_z" proven={{*}}|L0 writers-known
# HELD: "_w" proven={{*}}|L1 writers-known
# RUN(WALK): walk f6 mechanisms=all
# WALK-LABEL: code f6:Body
# WALK: GetSlot {{*}}key="n" receivers=[L0]
# WALK: GetSlot {{*}}key="n" receivers=[L1]
